# {{ spec.name }} — Agent Briefing

> Instructions for AI coding agents (Windsurf Cascade, Kilo CLI, Claude Code, etc.)
> **Client lane rules:** `.windsurf/rules/mobile-app/80-mobile.md` (+ `81-mobile-billing.md`).
> **Backend lane rules (Pattern-A FastAPI):** `10-python.md`, `30-ops.md`, `55-observability.md`.

This project is a **two-part scaffold**: an Expo/React-Native **client** at the repo root
(`src/`) and a bundled **FastAPI backend** under `server/` that deploys to the VPS via
`fabrik apply` (same Pattern-A shape as any other service). The client talks ONLY to that
backend over `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL`.

## Client stack (Expo SDK 57, New Architecture)

- **Expo SDK 57 / React 19 / React Native 0.81** — New Architecture (Fabric/JSI) is
  mandatory; never write legacy-bridge code.
- **Routing:** `expo-router` (file-based, under `src/app/`). NEVER add `@react-navigation/*`
  to app code — routing is the router's job.
- **Styling:** **Uniwind** (Tailwind v4, compiled at build time via the Expo bundler config).
  Design tokens live in `src/global.css` (`@theme`, Ocoron palette, dark-first). No raw hex in
  components; no `react-native-unistyles`/NativeWind. Details: `80-mobile.md`.
- **API client:** generated by `@hey-api/openapi-ts` from the backend's `openapi.json` into
  `src/lib/api/generated/` (regenerate with `pnpm generate-api`). NEVER hand-roll `axios` — call
  the typed hooks, never fetch from a screen.
- **Server state:** TanStack React Query, wrapped by the offline provider (`src/lib/offline/`,
  MMKV-persisted cache + NetInfo online-manager).
- **Storage:** `react-native-mmkv` v4 (`createMMKV()`, never `new MMKV()`) for fast non-sensitive
  KV; **`expo-secure-store` for JWTs/tokens — NEVER MMKV/AsyncStorage** (`src/lib/auth/utils.tsx`).
- **Analytics/consent:** `posthog-react-native`, opt-OUT by default (`defaultOptIn:false`); no
  capture until `optIn()` — the consent seam is `src/lib/consent/` (`hasAnalyticsConsent()`).
- **Force-update / kill-switch:** `src/lib/update/` calls `GET /app-config` and blocks entry when
  the server returns `update_required`/`kill_switch` (the server owns the semver — see below).
- **Crash reporting:** `@sentry/react-native` (`src/lib/crash.tsx`, DSN via `EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN`).
- **i18n:** `i18next` + `expo-localization`; strings synced by `scripts/sync_rn_locales.py`. No
  hardcoded user-facing strings.
- **Billing:** RevenueCat — see `81-mobile-billing.md`.

## Backend stack (Pattern-A FastAPI — `server/src/app/`)

- Minimal default: **NO database, NO auth** (`defaults.yaml` `shape.needs_database:false`,
  `has_bearer_api:false`). Opt into auth by vendoring `fabrik-lib/fastapi-user-auth` + `account`
  and flipping both flags.
- Routes: `GET /health` (liveness — never behind auth) and `GET /app-config` (force-update /
  kill-switch / feature-toggle gate). `/app-config` owns the semver comparison via the **vendored
  `mobile_config`** module (`server/src/mobile_config/`) — never re-implement version math in the
  client. Contract + request/response shape: `docs/reference/SEAMS.md`.
- Deploys via `fabrik apply`: the scaffolder emits the FastAPI `Dockerfile` (builds only `server/`,
  `uvicorn app.main:app`, port 8000) + a canonical `compose.yaml`. `.dockerignore` excludes the RN
  client so the image ships `server/` only.

## Seam map — where the `rn-*` kits bind

`docs/reference/SEAMS.md` is the source of truth. In brief: consent-state
(`hasAnalyticsConsent`), the hey-api client location, the Uniwind `@theme`, the
`expo-secure-store` auth store, and the backend route seams (`GET /app-config`, and the future
`GET /entitlements` / `POST /support` / presigned-upload / OAuth routes).

## Build & test

```bash
pnpm install                    # pnpm is the client package manager (preinstall enforces it)
pnpm start                      # expo start
pnpm ios                        # expo run:ios   (dev build; macOS)
pnpm android                    # expo run:android (dev build)
pnpm type-check                 # tsc --noEmit
pnpm test                       # jest-expo
pnpm lint
# backend: PYTHONPATH=server/src pytest server/tests   (venv: pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-dev.txt)
```

**Production binaries: cloud EAS only** — `eas build --profile production` (iOS + Android); profiles
in `eas.json`. No local release builds. First EAS build needs `assets/` icons + a splash and your own
EAS `projectId` + Expo account owner in `app.config.ts` (run `eas init` — the scaffold ships them blank).

## Project structure

```
src/app/            # expo-router routes (_layout.tsx wires the providers + ForceUpdateGate)
src/lib/            # api (generated hey-api), auth (secure-store), consent, offline, update, storage, crash
src/features/       # feature modules (auth, feed, settings, …)
src/global.css      # Uniwind @theme (Ocoron tokens, dark-first)
server/src/app/     # FastAPI backend (main, routes/health, routes/app_config)
server/src/mobile_config/   # vendored force-update/kill-switch module
server/tests/       # backend pytest (health + /app-config contract)
```

## Internal audit (mobile-specific)

- [ ] **JWTs in `expo-secure-store`**, never MMKV/AsyncStorage.
- [ ] **No `@react-navigation/*`** in app code (expo-router only).
- [ ] **No `axios.create`** — use the generated hey-api client.
- [ ] **mmkv v4** (`createMMKV`, never `new MMKV()`).
- [ ] **No raw hex** — Uniwind `@theme` tokens only.
- [ ] **No hardcoded user-facing strings** (i18n) and **no hardcoded secrets** (`EXPO_PUBLIC_*` = client-safe only).
- [ ] **Backend `/health` real** (probes deps when a DB is enabled); never behind auth.

